   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_dcmi.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   *          functionalities of the DCMI peripheral:           
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   *           + Image capture functions  
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   *
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****  @verbatim          
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****  ===============================================================================
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****  ===============================================================================  
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****     [..]       
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       The sequence below describes how to use this driver to capture image
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       from a camera module connected to the DCMI Interface.
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       This sequence does not take into account the configuration of the  
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       camera module, which should be made before to configure and enable
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       the DCMI to capture images.
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****              
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       (#) Enable the clock for the DCMI and associated GPIOs using the following 
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           functions:
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           RCC_AHB2PeriphClockCmd(RCC_AHB2Periph_DCMI, ENABLE);
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           RCC_AHB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_AHB1Periph_GPIOx, ENABLE);
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       (#) DCMI pins configuration 
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****         (++) Connect the involved DCMI pins to AF13 using the following function 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccdCpHpZ.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****             GPIO_PinAFConfig(GPIOx, GPIO_PinSourcex, GPIO_AF_DCMI); 
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****         (++) Configure these DCMI pins in alternate function mode by calling 
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****             the function GPIO_Init();
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       (#) Declare a DCMI_InitTypeDef structure, for example:
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           DCMI_InitTypeDef  DCMI_InitStructure;
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           and fill the DCMI_InitStructure variable with the allowed values
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           of the structure member.
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****     
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       (#) Initialize the DCMI interface by calling the function
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           DCMI_Init(&DCMI_InitStructure); 
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****     
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       (#) Configure the DMA2_Stream1 channel1 to transfer Data from DCMI DR
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           register to the destination memory buffer.
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****     
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       (#) Enable DCMI interface using the function
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           DCMI_Cmd(ENABLE);
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****                    
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       (#) Start the image capture using the function
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           DCMI_CaptureCmd(ENABLE);
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****                    
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       (#) At this stage the DCMI interface waits for the first start of frame,
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           then a DMA request is generated continuously/once (depending on the
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           mode used, Continuous/Snapshot) to transfer the received data into
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****           the destination memory. 
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****      
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****       -@-  If you need to capture only a rectangular window from the received
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****            image, you have to use the DCMI_CROPConfig() function to configure 
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****            the coordinates and size of the window to be captured, then enable 
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****            the Crop feature using DCMI_CROPCmd(ENABLE);  
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****            In this case, the Crop configuration should be made before to enable
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****            and start the DCMI interface. 
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c **** 
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****  @endverbatim     
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   ******************************************************************************
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dcmi.c ****   * @attention
